# Chrysalis

1. **Authoritative rules** are in **`AGENTS.md`**. Read **`DESIGN.md`**, **`docs/UNIVERSAL-TRANSLATOR-CANON.md`** (canon + **D6442** translate-only + **D6447** no demo-only), **`docs/STRATEGIC-PLAN.md`** (locked path — do not deviate), **`docs/MIGRATION-OS.md`** (operator stack), **`docs/PAUSED-AND-MAINTENANCE.md`** (maintenance + paused index), and **`ROADMAP.md`** as required there.
2. **True conversion only — never demo-only code (**D6447**).** Applies to **every language pair**, not WISP alone. Do not invent simplified login/dashboard/shells, parity façades, force-settled green holes, or helper apps that only look like the product. Lift origin or emit an honest hole. After convert: **sign in and test against origin**.
3. User messages without **build/implement/add/fix** are usually **questions** — clarify against the strategic plan; do not fork unless the user explicitly amends the plan. **Translate only** — do not invent map engines, CDN dialects, or chrome absent from source (**D6442**).
4. After substantive changes, run **`pnpm test`** (or the smallest relevant package tests). Respect package boundaries (no circular dependencies; no oracle or environment shortcuts in generated or verify code).
